  "published": "2026-06-11T18:57:04.71Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.2: RealTimeTrace.Stop() no longer zeroes the session handle when ControlTrace(STOP) fails — zeroing made every later Stop()/Dispose() a silent no-op and permanently orphaned the kernel-side session. Stop now treats ERROR_WMI_INSTANCE_NOT_FOUND as success, retries a failed handle-based stop by session name, and exposes the outcome via the new RealTimeTrace.LastStopStatus property.\nv2.0.1: Bump transitive symbolresolver dependency to 2.0.0 so consumers get the AOT/trim-compatible release (v2.0.0 shipped still pinning symbolresolver 1.3.0).\nv2.0.0: Retarget to net10.0-windows7.0. Migrate all P/Invoke from [DllImport] to [LibraryImport] source-generated marshalling for AOT compatibility. Marked IsAotCompatible + IsTrimmable. Public-API preserved — existing [UnmanagedFunctionPointer] delegate callbacks still work; callers should provide static callbacks for full AOT compatibility.",
